# Wave W17-Z (Lake Insight): warden post — a warden’s marker post at the honest-ice crossing’s shore: a snow-capped post flying one small rust pennant, the ice warden’s mark where the crossing is honest (design: the warden keeps the crossing; his tracks cross the preserved ice to this shore). On calm turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from Lake Gallant’s light posts by the pennant entire (those carry a lamp for open water; this carries a flag for ice) and from Route 217’s gear posts behind it by office: those serve climbers, this one serves the lake.
